{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1104841-hedge-magic-and-the-fae","id":1104841,"title":"Hedge Magic and the Fae","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-17T13:20:04-07:00","id":1104841,"title":"Hedge Magic and the Fae","content":"As written in past WW products, Numina/Hedge Magic have great potential in a Changeling setting. Especially in regards to kinain and enchanted mortals. <br /> <br /> Folklore is loaded with tales of minor magicians who deal with the fae. Skillymen, wise-folk and hedge mages. These were not folk who called storms or flew, but they did get back stolen children and dealt with unruly house sprites.<br /> <br /> Though taking from Sorcerer is easy enough, not everything lines up well with Changeling. So I wonder about some Changeling Hedge Magic. Some simple magical arts that access the dreaming in specific ways, but not as versatile as Arts and Realms.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 06-17-2017, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T14:25:14-07:00","id":1104861,"title":"","content":"Take a good look at <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Rite\" target=\"_blank\">Rites</a>.<br /> <br /> Gremayre or similar skill to perform.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 06-17-2017, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T14:29:52-07:00","id":1104862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1104841-hedge-magic-and-the-fae?p=1104861#post1104861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take a good look at <a href=\"http://&amp;quot;http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Rite&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Rites</a>.<br /> <br /> Gremayre or similar skill to perform.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sort of thing might do. Changeling Oaths give a good hint as to what is possible. But what might mortal magicians do?<br /> <br /> Possible Riuals: Dowsing, Fae Rhymes, Cleansings, Luck Charms, Love, Herbal Potions, etc.<br /> <br /> Fun ponderings to ponder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 06-18-2017, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T18:03:30-07:00","id":1104938,"title":"","content":"I like kinians and enchanted wisemen and women, they can do magical things. I'm not so good on making new magic paths, been stuck trying to balance one. But what about a hedge magic based around the use of a Narrative? I know it could possibly end up as a mixture of path abilities but fairy tales all have a narrative, so why couldnt a magi make one where chimeras and changelings are pulled to go along with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T23:33:10-07:00","id":1104992,"title":"","content":"There was a really kickass Wyrdmagic on the forum for Changeling the Lost that enchanted could use. But for Dreaming I figured the most common I assumed were Alchemy and Enchantment, followed by Oneiromancy, Ritual Summoning/binding/Warding, Weather, and Divination. You Sorcery system wise is all the same so you could use Fae Foci and resonance for their sorcerers.<br /> <br /> I always wondered when a Changeling has a chimerical Death and they forget their magical lives, what about if they learned sorcery and met other magical beings? How do they explain why they are say an expert at ancient and arcane blacksmithing or alchemy? They must be very confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T05:58:35-07:00","id":1105045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1104841-hedge-magic-and-the-fae?p=1104992#post1104992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a really kickass Wyrdmagic on the forum for Changeling the Lost that enchanted could use. But for Dreaming I figured the most common I assumed were Alchemy and Enchantment, followed by Oneiromancy, Ritual Summoning/binding/Warding, Weather, and Divination. You Sorcery system wise is all the same so you could use Fae Foci and resonance for their sorcerers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Overall, I am torn between Paths/Psychic Powers and just making a list of minor Rituals/Spells that can be purchased as a background. For such spells I would balance them much like Chimerical Redes, using Trait + Gramayre for a dice pool. But for Paths, I would think Alchemy (of use to Changelings as well), Conjuring, Divination, Ephemera and similar low profile magics (the kind you see at a Psychic Fair or a Travelling Medicine Show) would be best. <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Oneiromancy </span></span></span>is neat, but could be confused with the Art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 06-18-2017, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T07:55:42-07:00","id":1105079,"title":"","content":"For Oneiromancy, you could use Rites+Lucid Dreaming skill.<br /> <br /> I could argue, that Sorcerer's Oneiromancy is even better, than Changeling's one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T09:16:02-07:00","id":1105093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1104841-hedge-magic-and-the-fae?p=1105079#post1105079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Oneiromancy, you could use Rites+Lucid Dreaming skill.<br /> <br /> I could argue, that Sorcerer's Oneiromancy is even better, than Changeling's one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Its that &quot;same name different results&quot; thing that makes me thoughtful. That perhaps some setting specific paths are called for. Dream Travel, Oathbinding/taking, Riddle-rhyme, Herbcraft etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T12:49:32-07:00","id":1105143,"title":"","content":"Definitely NOT a Herbcraft. =)<br /> <br /> Stick to the folklore is my advice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T15:15:32-07:00","id":1105196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1104841-hedge-magic-and-the-fae?p=1105143#post1105143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely NOT a Herbcraft. =)<br /> <br /> Stick to the folklore is my advice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Joking, right?<br /> <br /> Herbcraft is a major component of fairy folklore. Including mortal folk magic concerning them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 06-18-2017, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T16:31:18-07:00","id":1105216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1104841-hedge-magic-and-the-fae?p=1105196#post1105196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Joking, right?<br /> <br /> Herbcraft is a major component of fairy folklore. Including mortal folk magic concerning them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm about 99,7% sure it was not, how it was called. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T07:53:21-07:00","id":1114587,"title":"","content":"For an interesting take on Mortal Hedge Magicians in a Changeling game. This is an excerpt from the &quot;Dark Ages Tome of Secrets&quot; page 71-75 (a wonderful book). I think this sort of thing would be a marvelous addition to Changeling. Simple magics that could be found among all manner of persons that Changelings may interact with. From carnival folk, faith healers and, stage magicians to true occultists and soothsayers. <br /> <br /> Following these parameters, what fae-inspired Incantations might be created?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Incantations</b><br /> An Incantation is a bundle of strictly circumscribed magical potential, unlocked by a precise mix of materials, conditions, and ritual acts. A magician needs time and discipline to master an Incantation, but doesn\u2019t need a special soul, second sight, or any sort of enlightenment. An exceptional magician might command a handful of Incantations, but knowing even one is enough to make her notably powerful.<br /> An Incantation is a bit of magic bound up in the world. Each one completes a simple task so long as the magician performs its required ritual perfectly, and with supreme focus. Where many of a magician\u2019s other abilities rely on intuition, Incantations re\u00adquire rote learning to perform correctly. They permit only the slightest stylistic flourishes \u2014 a cry to Mary instead of The Morrigan, perhaps \u2014 and so require investment in a Mental Merit: Incantation<br /> <br /> <b>Incantation (2 Pt. Supernatural Merit) </b><br /> Your character learns a single Incantation. This Merit may be purchased during play several times, each for a new Incantation. This costs six experience points.<br /> <br /> <b>Incantation Procedure </b><br /> Once the character learns an Incantation, he may use it by following this procedure:<br /> <b>Ritual Requirements: </b>Each Incantation can only be cast in a particular time, place, or both, such as at under the full moon or at a murderer\u2019s grave. The Incantation also requires specific materials: certain herbs, say, or worms boiled in a cauldron. Only then can the magician perform ritual acts to rouse the Incantation\u2019s magic.<br /> <b>Circle, Amulet, or Potion: </b>The magician must decide whether the Incantation\u2019s power affects an area (circle), is bound to an object that can be moved (amulet), or is stored within an object that is later consumed (potion). Incantations possess one great limit compared to other forms of magic, in that they cannot truly affect distant targets unless an amulet or potion is brought to its location. The exception is To Summon a Being, which draws the target to a location. Note that \u201ccircle,\u201d \u201camulet,\u201d and \u201cpotion\u201d are examples and general names, and a length of red string that expends its magic when tied to someone might count as a \u201cpotion\u201d for rules purposes. A circle need not be truly circular, but can define a space with no more than a 50- foot radius. An amulet is transferrable, and can be stolen from or secreted on a person.<br /> <b>Willpower Expenditure and Roll: </b>At the ritual\u2019s con\u00adclusion, spend one point of the magician\u2019s Willpower and roll her permanent Willpower (difficulty 8). Only one success is required to bring about the Incantation\u2019s full effect. Additional successes may only be useful if some supernat\u00adural power might interfere with the Incantation, in which case the successes scored serve as a general measurement of its strength.<br /> If the roll fails, nothing happens, but the materials are no longer fit for the Incantation, and must be replaced if the magician wants to make another attempt.<br /> On a botch, malformed magic ripples through the magician, causing sudden pain and illness. This inflicts one level of aggravated damage and leaves a mortal bedridden for a few days.<br /> <b>Incantations and Other Magic: </b>Incantations cannot undo the effects of Path magic, Cantrips, and Awakened magic. They\u2019re inferior to all of these, and these forms of magic can undo Incantations using their usual systems for countermagic, as if each Incantation were a one-dot power that scored one success.<br /> <br /> <b>Sample Incantations</b><br /> The following Incantations represent a small sample of those learned by magicians, and have been selected because the fae may find them of interest. Design more using these as examples.<br /> <br /> <b>For Luck </b><br /> Magicians shift fate with this Incantation, calling on saints or gods to reorder the normal course of destiny.<br /> <b>Ritual Requirements: </b>The magician defines one narrow circumstance (\u201cin battle with a sword,\u201d or \u201cwhen I argue with the tax collector,\u201d for example) while inscribing the names or symbols of powers that will intercede for the beneficiary. The ritual must be cast outdoors, but out of sight of the stars \u2014 heavy clouds are typically required.<br /> <b>System: </b>Cast in a circle, the Incantation benefits one person of the magician\u2019s choice for activities taking place within it, granting a \u20132 reduction on the difficulty of dice rolls related to the circumstance three times, each chosen by the beneficiary\u2019s player. An amulet provides this same benefit to anyone wearing it. A potion gives the imbiber one automatic success, which can be stacked with personal Willpower expenditure, on one future, applicable dice roll of the beneficiary\u2019s choice.<br /> <br /> <b>For Wounds</b><br /> This Incantation treats serious wounds. It can even knit and smooth the dead flesh of Cainites, though it is less potent than the power in their blood.<br /> <b>Ritual Requirements: </b>In all cases, the magician must ac\u00adquire the source of the injury: ash from a fire that burned the victim, or a weapon that struck her. (Thus, it can\u2019t be used in cases of immaterial or very distant sources of injury, such as body-ripping magic or the sun.) In a magic circle, the magician touches the source to the victim. In the case of a potion (usually a poultice, actually) someone (not necessarily the witch) must touch the source of harm to the potion before the injured party imbibes it. Once cast, the Incantation must be used before the following midnight.<br /> <b>System: </b>The Incantation heals one level of aggravated damage or two levels of lethal damage. <br /> <br /> <b>To Find Treasure </b><br /> Magicians are often called on to find wealth left by dead relations, hidden vaults, or thieves. This is a well-known Incantation not only because of its utility, but because magicians pretend to know it to bilk fools out of coins, because it takes money to find it. Despite the name, the Incantation can be used to find items with no monetary value, but not the living or undead.<br /> <b>Ritual Requirements: </b>Under the full moon, the magician burns or buries an example of the treasure being sought: Silver dollars for vaults or a key for a strongbox, for instance. It need not come from the source being sought, but should have two points of association (an old key for an old strongbox, etc). Fraudsters typically ask for more money, and only pretend to destroy it.<br /> <b>System: </b>Cast in a circle, the Incantation gives the witch a vision of the treasure\u2019s exact location, if it lies within the circle\u2019s bounds, and a rough idea of how to get to it (if it must be dug up or sits in a chest, for instance). A potion gives its user a vision of the nearest items of that type and its immediate surroundings, along with its direction at the time the potion was consumed, but no other information. An amulet pulls in the direction of the nearest items of that type, but provides no other information. The amulet continues to possess this power until its bearer touches or sees treasure of this type, or until the next full moon. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}